        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Pascal's Law states that pressure applied to a confined fluid is transmitted undiminished throughout the fluid. In a hydraulic brake system, this principle allows the force applied at the brake pedal to be transmitted to the brake pads at each wheel.</p>",
